From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 04:59:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/56] feat(ui): the reviewer layout keeps to reviewing

A review of the reviewer layout's controls, state by state, asked for less:
only the Hand and Comment in the dock, nothing of the agents, no design
tokens, the pages instead of the layer tree, and one bar on a phone. The
layout is for people who look and comment; agents design over MCP.

With FULL_UI off and the floating panel layout:

- The dock's tools are the Hand and Comment. The More tools menu is gone.
  A tool picked by its key (V, R, ...) shows as a pressed button in the
  tool group while it is active, and a click on it goes back to the Hand.
  Prototype mode, when it is on, shows the same way, as a way out.
- No AI activity and no Connect AI, on the desktop dock and in the phone's
  canvas actions. The side panel is the comments alone: no Tasks, Activity
  or Memory tabs, no memory proposal pill or decision toast, no "working
  now" line, and Cmd+K does not open the agent composer.
- The left panel is the pages, the panel's full height, with its collapse
  button in the heading. The layer tree and the Tokens tab are gone, with
  their rail buttons; tokens stay reachable to agents over MCP. The fold
  between Pages and Layers (and its two strings) is removed.
- A phone has one bar: back, Hand, Comment | zoom level | Comments, Pages,
  ...  The floating zoom pill's -/+ and the Present button at the top
  right go; Present is the first item of the canvas actions sheet.

Everything comes back with the docked panel layout (Settings, Appearance)
or with localStorage doop:full-ui='on' and a reload.

Tests: reviewerLayoutBrowser (the dock's two tools, a key-picked tool and
its way back, Prototype mode only while on, pages alone, one comments tab)
and phoneReviewBrowser (one bar: the zoom level in the dock, no -/+, no
Present on screen).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
